==Battleground==
*10 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 1.33~3.33 seconds<sup>40f~100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 97% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 96% HP:
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 95% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 93% HP:
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 92% HP:
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.67~3.33 seconds<sup>20f~100f</sup>.
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.

==Strategy==
There are two ways to deal with this stage. The first is to carefully spawn the enemies one at a time, while the second and least efficient is to hit the base hard and deal with all the enemies at once. Of course, you want the first thing to happen; for this to be possible, it's important to have [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]] (or [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Cow]] if in {{4c}}) in your army, this way you can hit the base lightly after killing each enemy.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
Enemy density is low here, so strong [[Single Attack]] units can perfom especially well in this stage. Obvious examples of this are [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Islands]]. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge]] can hamper the pushing power of all the enemies here, while [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] can eliminate it outright.

==='''Strategy 1 ([[Cheese]])'''===
Since this stage has an enemy limit of 10 and spawns 10 Wall Doges at the start, you can cheese it by spawning [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cats]] to stall the Wall Doges and using the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] to knock the Wall Doges behind the base. After that, you can spawn an [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to finish off the base. This cheese does not work with Awakened Bahamut's Explosion Talent, as he will kill all the Wall Doges. This cheese is primarily meant for {{4c}} players. You can also use units such as [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan Pasalan]] to knock the Wall Doges back faster.

